{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "a3f2c1d4-8b7e-4f9a-bc12-3e5d7a9f0123",
    "name": "Webbeet UX Audit Tool",
    "description": "# Webbeet UX Audit Tool API\n\nScores a website across 6 categories: Performance, SEO, Trust, UX Signals, Mobile, and Accessibility.\n\n---\n\n## ⚠️ Important: Postman timeout\n\nGo to **Postman Settings → General → Request timeout** and set it to **120000** (120s). The audit can take 40-90s for larger sites.\n\n---\n\n## Streaming response format\n\nSuccessful audits return `text/event-stream` (Server-Sent Events). The response body contains two events:\n\n```\ndata: {\"type\":\"partial\",\"categories\":{\"seo\":{...},\"trust\":{...},\"ux\":{...}}}\n\ndata: {\"type\":\"complete\",\"categories\":{\"performance\":{...},\"mobile\":{...},\"accessibility\":{...}},\"overallScore\":72,\"shareId\":\"abc123\",\"scannedAt\":\"...\"}\n```\n\n**Phase 1 - partial** (~3-5s): Fast HTML-based checks: SEO (13), Trust (7), UX (9) = 29 checks.\n\n**Phase 2 - complete** (~15-90s): PageSpeed + accessibility checks: Performance (8), Mobile (6), Accessibility (8) = 22 checks.\n\nTotal across both phases = **51 checks**.\n\n---\n\n## Error responses (plain JSON - before stream starts)\n\n```json\n{ \"error\": \"Please enter a valid website URL including https://\" }\n```\n\nStatus codes: `400` (bad input), `422` (unreachable/blocked), `429` (rate limited)\n\n---\n\n## Check status values\n- `pass` - all good\n- `warning` - needs attention  \n- `fail` - significant issue\n\n## Score bands\n- 80-100 - Good\n- 50-79 - Needs work\n- 0-49 - Poor",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "base_url",
      "value": "http://localhost:3000",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Switch to https://ux-audit.exlinelabs.co.uk for production"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Happy Path",
      "description": "Successful audits. Response is SSE (text/event-stream) - two data: lines containing JSON events.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Audit - webbeet.studio",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "// ── Parse SSE events from response body ───────────────────",
                  "// The API returns text/event-stream with two events:",
                  "//   data: {type:'partial', categories:{seo,trust,ux}}",
                  "//   data: {type:'complete', categories:{performance,mobile,accessibility}, overallScore, shareId}",
                  "",
                  "const text = pm.response.text();",
                  "const events = [];",
                  "text.split('\\n').forEach(line => {",
                  "    if (line.startsWith('data: ')) {",
                  "        try { events.push(JSON.parse(line.slice(6))); } catch(e) {}",
                  "    }",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "const partial  = events.find(e => e.type === 'partial');",
                  "const complete = events.find(e => e.type === 'complete');",
                  "",
                  "// ── Response shape ────────────────────────────────────────",
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Content-Type is text/event-stream', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('Content-Type')).to.include('text/event-stream');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Got partial event (Phase 1 - HTML checks)', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(partial).to.not.be.undefined;",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Got complete event (Phase 2 - PageSpeed + a11y)', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(complete).to.not.be.undefined;",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "// ── Phase 1 checks ────────────────────────────────────────",
                  "if (partial) {",
                  "    pm.test('Partial has seo, trust, ux categories', () => {",
                  "        ['seo','trust','ux'].forEach(c => {",
                  "            pm.expect(partial.categories).to.have.property(c);",
                  "        });",
                  "    });",
                  "    pm.test('Partial has 29 checks total', () => {",
                  "        const total = Object.values(partial.categories)",
                  "            .reduce((n, cat) => n + (cat.checks ? cat.checks.length : 0), 0);",
                  "        pm.expect(total).to.equal(29);",
                  "    });",
                  "}",
                  "",
                  "// ── Phase 2 checks ────────────────────────────────────────",
                  "if (complete) {",
                  "    pm.test('Complete has performance, mobile, accessibility', () => {",
                  "        ['performance','mobile','accessibility'].forEach(c => {",
                  "            pm.expect(complete.categories).to.have.property(c);",
                  "        });",
                  "    });",
                  "    pm.test('overallScore is 0-100', () => {",
                  "        pm.expect(complete.overallScore).to.be.a('number');",
                  "        pm.expect(complete.overallScore).to.be.within(0, 100);",
                  "    });",
                  "    pm.test('scannedAt is present', () => {",
                  "        pm.expect(complete.scannedAt).to.be.a('string');",
                  "    });",
                  "    pm.test('shareId returned (Supabase connected)', () => {",
                  "        // Will pass only if Supabase env vars are set",
                  "        pm.expect(complete.shareId).to.be.a('string');",
                  "    });",
                  "    pm.test('Each check has id, label, value, status, description', () => {",
                  "        Object.values(complete.categories).forEach(cat => {",
                  "            if (!cat.checks) return;",
                  "            cat.checks.forEach(check => {",
                  "                pm.expect(check).to.have.all.keys('id','label','value','status','description');",
                  "                pm.expect(['pass','warning','fail']).to.include(check.status);",
                  "            });",
                  "        });",
                  "    });",
                  "}",
                  "",
                  "// ── Console summary ───────────────────────────────────────",
                  "if (complete) {",
                  "    console.log('Overall score:', complete.overallScore);",
                  "    if (partial) {",
                  "        Object.entries(partial.categories).forEach(([k,v]) => {",
                  "            console.log(' [phase1]', k + ':', v.score, '(' + (v.checks||[]).length + ' checks)');",
                  "        });",
                  "    }",
                  "    Object.entries(complete.categories).forEach(([k,v]) => {",
                  "        const tag = v.unavailable ? '(unavailable)' : '(' + (v.checks||[]).length + ' checks)';",
                  "        console.log(' [phase2]', k + ':', v.unavailable ? 'N/A' : v.score, tag);",
                  "    });",
                  "    console.log('shareId:', complete.shareId || 'none (Supabase not connected)');",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n    \"url\": \"https://webbeet.studio\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/audit",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["api", "audit"]
            },
            "description": "Full audit of webbeet.studio. Expect two SSE events in the response body - partial (Phase 1, ~5s) and complete (Phase 2, ~20s). Overall 51 checks across 6 categories."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Audit - stripe.com (medium complexity)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const text = pm.response.text();",
                  "const events = [];",
                  "text.split('\\n').forEach(line => {",
                  "    if (line.startsWith('data: ')) {",
                  "        try { events.push(JSON.parse(line.slice(6))); } catch(e) {}",
                  "    }",
                  "});",
                  "const partial  = events.find(e => e.type === 'partial');",
                  "const complete = events.find(e => e.type === 'complete');",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Got both SSE events', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(partial).to.not.be.undefined;",
                  "    pm.expect(complete).to.not.be.undefined;",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('overallScore is a number', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(complete?.overallScore).to.be.a('number');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "if (complete) {",
                  "    console.log('stripe.com overall:', complete.overallScore);",
                  "    if (partial) Object.entries(partial.categories).forEach(([k,v]) => console.log(' [phase1]', k + ':', v.score));",
                  "    Object.entries(complete.categories).forEach(([k,v]) => {",
                  "        console.log(' [phase2]', k + ':', v.unavailable ? 'unavailable' : v.score);",
                  "    });",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n    \"url\": \"https://stripe.com\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/audit",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["api", "audit"]
            },
            "description": "Medium-complexity site. Expect 51 checks. PageSpeed typically takes 35-55s for Stripe."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Audit - github.com (large/heavy site)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const text = pm.response.text();",
                  "const events = [];",
                  "text.split('\\n').forEach(line => {",
                  "    if (line.startsWith('data: ')) {",
                  "        try { events.push(JSON.parse(line.slice(6))); } catch(e) {}",
                  "    }",
                  "});",
                  "const partial  = events.find(e => e.type === 'partial');",
                  "const complete = events.find(e => e.type === 'complete');",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Phase 1 (HTML checks) always arrives', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(partial).to.not.be.undefined;",
                  "    const checks = Object.values(partial?.categories || {})",
                  "        .reduce((n, c) => n + (c.checks||[]).length, 0);",
                  "    pm.expect(checks).to.equal(29);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Phase 2 arrives (PageSpeed may mark performance as unavailable for very large sites)', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(complete).to.not.be.undefined;",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "if (complete) {",
                  "    const perf = complete.categories?.performance;",
                  "    if (perf?.unavailable) {",
                  "        console.log('Performance: unavailable (PageSpeed timed out for this site - normal for very large sites)');",
                  "    } else {",
                  "        console.log('Performance score:', perf?.score);",
                  "    }",
                  "    console.log('Overall score:', complete.overallScore, '(calculated from available categories)');",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n    \"url\": \"https://github.com\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/audit",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["api", "audit"]
            },
            "description": "Heavy site - tests that large sites always return Phase 1 results even if PageSpeed is slow. Performance/mobile may show as 'unavailable' if PageSpeed exceeds its 90s timeout. Increase Postman timeout to 120s in settings."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Audit - HTTP site (HTTPS check should fail)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const text = pm.response.text();",
                  "const events = [];",
                  "text.split('\\n').forEach(line => {",
                  "    if (line.startsWith('data: ')) {",
                  "        try { events.push(JSON.parse(line.slice(6))); } catch(e) {}",
                  "    }",
                  "});",
                  "const partial = events.find(e => e.type === 'partial');",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('HTTPS trust check is fail', () => {",
                  "    const trustChecks = partial?.categories?.trust?.checks ?? [];",
                  "    const httpsCheck = trustChecks.find(c => c.id === 'https');",
                  "    pm.expect(httpsCheck, 'https check missing').to.not.be.undefined;",
                  "    pm.expect(httpsCheck?.status).to.equal('fail');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n    \"url\": \"http://neverssl.com\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/audit",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["api", "audit"]
            },
            "description": "neverssl.com is a real HTTP-only site kept intentionally unsecure. The trust category's 'https' check should have status:'fail'."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
